  "description": "Creation of a dropped kerb vehicle crossover",
  "development_type": "Certificates of Lawful Development",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The purpose of the proposed dropped kerb vehicular crossover is to serve an existing maisonette/ leasehold flat (no 51 Bransby Road). A maisonette or flat does not benefit from permitted development rights as it does not constitute a single dwellinghouse for the purposes of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended). Permitted development rights under Schedule 2, Part 1 applies only to dwellinghouses and expressly excluded flats and maisonettes. Therefore, as development, within the meaning of Section 55 of The Town and Country Planning Act 1990,   is proposed planning permission would be required."
  ],
